# Manual SQL and Local Infrastructure

- Do not add Flyway, Liquibase, Testcontainers, embedded databases or application-startup schema creation.
- Keep each service's current DDL in a reviewed plain SQL file that an operator applies manually.
- Keep all required initial DML for one service in one reviewed SQL file; do not rebuild seed data through Java object graphs.
- Java startup may validate connectivity but must not create, migrate, repair or seed business data.
- Tests reuse the repository-owned services from `local-environment`; they do not start or stop containers.
- A missing local dependency must fail fast and print the exact setup command or documentation path.
- Tests may clean only rows and namespaces they own. Never drop a shared schema, flush a shared database or destroy Docker volumes.
- Keep production SQL, Mapper mappings, DataObjects and full-chain tests synchronized in the same change.
